WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.200
-Thanks for coming on the show.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.234
-Thank you for having me.
I love being here.

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:05.200
-Oh, please. I want to
congratulate you

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.100
on so many things.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.801
I just want to start
with "West Side Story" --

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:11.367
uh, you --

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.234
-Thank you.
-Not too shabby.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:16.234
You filmed that three years ago?
-Yeah, I was 16.

00:00:16.234 --> 00:00:18.434
-In New York?
-Yeah, it was crazy.

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.067
It's kind of
a full circle moment

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:22.067
to have it come out now
in New York.

00:00:22.067 --> 00:00:24.167
It's so cool.
I'm so happy to be a part of it.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:26.634
-Do you remember
the audition for that?

00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:29.200
-Yeah, I remember auditioning
in L.A. and I was thinking like,

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.267
"Oh, I'll just go do it,

00:00:30.267 --> 00:00:31.934
just because it's
a cool experience --

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:34.667
any dancer's dream to audition
for "West Side Story."

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.467
And then I got there,
did the audition.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:39.400
Went good, but I was like,
"That was fun. That was cool."

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.901
Didn't hear anything
for a little bit

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:43.534
and then flew back to New York,
got a callback,

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:46.734
and then walk in and
Steven Spielberg's in the room.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:49.701
I was like, "Oh, cool. So this
is, like, the final audition."

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:51.133
-Yeah.
-Like, "I made it this far."

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:52.667
-You're like, are you the real
Steven Spielberg?

00:00:52.667 --> 00:00:53.767
-Yeah.
-This is cool.

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:55.767
-I was like, "Cool, OK,
this is fun."

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.267
Also, I was, like,
one of the youngest ones,

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:59.501
so I was just kind of, like,
trying to soak it all in.

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:02.167
And then some time passed again,

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:05.100
and my agent called me
on, like, around Thanksgiving,

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.133
or maybe it was
Thanksgiving Day, and was, like,

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:08.767
"Yeah, so, like, we actually
heard back

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:11.100
from 'West Side Story,'" like,
"I'm really sorry,

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.267
you got the part."
And I was, like... [ screams ]

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:14.767
-Oh, yeah.
Hey, oh, heart attack.

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.767
-I literally had a heart attack.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:18.300
-I was like, "Cool, thank you,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.968
but also, I'm kind of, like,
traumatized."

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:21.400
-Don't ever do that again, yeah.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.033
-And then I was, like, "Oh,
I'm going to prank my mom now

00:01:23.033 --> 00:01:24.367
and do the same exact thing."

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.901
Because I like, "This is
actually kind of funny."

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.067
-[ Laughs ]
-So then --

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.868
-So then I did it exactly
to my mom.

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.100
-Yeah, just told your mom
you had bad news.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.067
-And she was, like, tears.
So yeah, it was fun.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:35.701
-Well, here's a picture of you
and Steven on set.

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:39.701
I will say, the choreography
on this movie,

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:41.300
it's the most insane thing...

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:42.667
-Justin Peck is a genius.

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.334
-I've ever seen in my life.

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:49.567
I go, I -- It almost looks like
it's the same person 400 times.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:51.000
-Everyone is so synchronized,

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.634
but has their own, like,
special --

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.400
-Different colors
and their own special thing.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.400
And it's like it's --
it's amazing.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.200
-Totally.
-You go, "What, that's not CGI?"

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.834
-Oh, definitely not.
Every dancer was, like,

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:03.534
so hardworking and so incredible
and so talented.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:04.901
So it was just cool to be
a part of it.

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:06.701
Do the --
I know the actors, too.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:09.300
I mean, do you get nervous
when you're having to act

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.901
in front of Steven Spielberg
and dance?

00:02:10.901 --> 00:02:12.434
-Oh, my God, are you kidding?
I --

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:14.000
I was having a heart attack
the whole time.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.200
-Yeah, you're, like,
"Can you please leave?"

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.400
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.734
-Do you mind just, like,
taking five over there?

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:19.300
-Please leave, Steven, thanks.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:20.667
We'll take it from here.
I know it's your movie,

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:21.901
but yeah, I don't want to do it
in front of you.

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:23.267
-Thanks for letting us be here,
though.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:24.334
-I appreciate it.
-Yeah.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:26.400
-Uh, love "Jaws." Yeah.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:29.300
-Literally.
-Yeah, right?

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.200
-No, it was --
he actually made it

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.534
such an amazing environment.

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:35.033
He was just as excited
as we all were,

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:36.734
like, literally watching
the monitor,

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:39.000
jumping up and down,
so excited.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.300
Like, it was his baby,
and I'm just so happy that he,

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.300
like, absolutely loved every bit
of the experience as well.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.834
-That's pretty cool.

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:48.801
Did he want you to sing
in the movie?

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.934
-Um, I don't sing.

00:02:50.934 --> 00:02:53.901
That's like a very known thing,
I think.

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:56.200
-Why?
-I -- You know...

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.000
I've learned --
I've come to the conclusion

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.501
that it's OK to not
be good at everything.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:02.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.000
And I've -- I've settled on,

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.434
"I'm not tone deaf,
and that's all that matters."

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:07.067
-OK. All right.
Well, yeah, but --

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.534
your boyfriend, though,
Eddie Benjamin needs --

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:11.033
-He's here.
-He's here tonight.

00:03:11.033 --> 00:03:14.067
Yeah, he's backstage. But
he's -- he's a great singer.

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:15.567
I mean, but --
-He's amazing.

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:17.133
I will not sing in front of him.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:18.934
Don't even ask me.
I never will.

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.067
-He's like Spielberg?

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:21.200
You're going to go
"Get out of the room?"

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.701
-Yeah, literally.
-I want to sing this song.

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.634
-But no, he doesn't. He doesn't
go, "Hey, just come on.

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:26.167
Let's just do this one song
together or something."

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:28.767
-Uh, you know, he's like,
"I could teach you.

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.334
I could -- like, I know you're
going to have to

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.000
do a role one day where you're
going to have to sing."

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:34.133
I'm, like, "No, I'll probably
have to turn it down

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:35.934
because that's how bad it is."

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:38.968
-No, there's no way.
-No, but he's there in case,

00:03:38.968 --> 00:03:40.901
you know, one day maybe --

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.033
-Training.
-Yeah.

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:43.634
-He's going on tour
with Justin Bieber.

00:03:43.634 --> 00:03:45.734
-Yes, he is.
-Now, this is a big deal.

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:47.200
-A huge deal.
-Yeah.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:49.400
-I mean, obviously, I was, like,
the biggest Justin Bieber fan

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.300
when I was younger.
I mean, everyone was, like --

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.601
-Hello, I'm the biggest -- yeah.
-Yeah, of course.

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:55.434
-I was a Belieber since day 1.
-I was a Belieber, yeah.

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.033
-Totally.
-Yeah.

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:59.200
Yeah, so it's, like,
a very full-circle moment.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.033
I actually met him
when I was, like, 8 years old

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:03.400
with my dance group,
which is so weird.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.601
We were like beside ourselves.
It was the coolest.

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:07.000
-What was he like?

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.801
-I -- I actually don't even
remember. I was star-struck.

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:11.100
-Really?
-Yeah, totally.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.467
-Like... [stammers]

00:04:12.467 --> 00:04:14.200
-I don't even -- I think it
happened so quickly.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:17.067
We were just all crying,
and then that was it.

00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:19.701
So, yeah.
He was really cute, though.

00:04:19.701 --> 00:04:21.868
-Oh, yeah, he's a good guy.
Are you going to go on tour?

00:04:21.868 --> 00:04:24.767
-Oh, definitely. I definitely
would love to see Justin,

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:27.701
of course, but I cannot wait to
watch Eddie perform.

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:29.100
-That's what I'm talking about.
-I'm so excited.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.234
-I'm going to be, like,
the groupie,

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:31.601
just, like, following along
everywhere.

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:32.701
-I love you!
-Yeah.

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:34.300
-No, I really do.
We love each other.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.767
-Yes. [ Laughs ]
-Hiya.

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:36.934
I'm like, "That's my boyfriend!"

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:38.701
-That's my boyfriend!
-Yeah.

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:39.968
I want to talk
about "The Fallout."

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:41.200
-Yes.
-Congratulations on this.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.267
-Thank you.
-Rave reviews.

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:43.467
It won the Grand Jury Prize.

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:44.801
-Thank you.

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:46.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:49.601
Won the Grand Jury Prize for
best film at SXSW.

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.033
-So crazy.
-It's massive.

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:52.567
-It's -- [stammers]

00:04:52.567 --> 00:04:55.000
-It's a beautiful movie.
Can you explain

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.501
what "The Fallout" is about?

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:58.801
-Yeah. "The Fallout" is
a coming-of-age story

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:01.300
about high schoolers
who share a unique bond,

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.567
and they're kind of navigating
love and self-discovery

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:07.200
and healing, kind of
in the aftermath of a tragedy

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.467
that happens at the school.

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:09.467
-Yeah.
-So yeah, it's --

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:11.267
it's a heavy one, for sure.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:13.801
-And is it true that I heard
that you improvised some scenes?

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:15.567
-Yeah, a lot of the time,

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:18.300
Megan -- the director and
writer, she's incredible,

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:20.634
and she was an actor previously,
so she definitely, like,

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:23.400
just let us do our thing,
which was amazing.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.934
And at the end of each scene,
she'd be, like,

00:05:24.934 --> 00:05:26.834
"Let's just do a fun run.
You guys do whatever you want."

00:05:26.834 --> 00:05:28.868
And a lot of those scenes ended
up making the movie

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:31.701
just because...
-It makes it so real.

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:33.667
And it's really --
it's great.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:34.901
-Thank you.
-Great performance. Congrats.

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:35.968
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.534
Here's Maddie Ziegler
in "The Fallout."

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:38.601
Take a look at this.

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:39.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:42.033
-You're, like, yodeling.

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:43.701
-You probably don't know this
about me,

00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:45.667
but I'm the best yodeler
in my family.

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:47.200
-Prove it.
-But --

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.434
You can't put me on the spot
like that,

00:05:49.434 --> 00:05:50.501
'cause then that's just, like,
you know --

00:05:50.501 --> 00:05:51.534
-This is, like,
the little preview.

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:53.234
-Yeah, this is, like, warm up.
-OK.

00:05:53.234 --> 00:05:56.100
-You know, but I'm going to get
you when you're not even ready,

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.767
and you're going to be, like...
[gasps dramatically]

00:05:58.767 --> 00:06:01.033
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:04.434
-Hey, you know, this might sound
weird because, like,

00:06:04.434 --> 00:06:05.767
I haven't known you
for that long,

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:09.100
but, like, I feel
so comfortable with you.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.901
Like, we're bonded or something.

00:06:13.334 --> 00:06:15.400
-Same.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.067
-Maddie Ziegler, everybody.

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:20.634
"The Fallout" premiers
January 27th on HBO Max.

